{
  "id": "27775_hiku",
  "headword": "{轢|ひ}く",
  "reading": "ひく",
  "romaji": "hiku",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to run over; to hit (with a vehicle)",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to run over; to hit (with a vehicle)",
      "explanation": "For a vehicle to strike a person or animal and pass over them. Always refers to a vehicle causing injury or death."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "27775_hiku_ex1",
      "japanese": "{車|くるま}が{猫|ねこ}を{轢|ひ}いた。",
      "english": "A car ran over a cat.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27775_hiku_ex2",
      "japanese": "{人|ひと}を{轢|ひ}いてしまわないよう{慎重|しんちょう}に{運転|うんてん}する。",
      "english": "I drive carefully so as not to run anyone over.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27775_hiku_ex3",
      "japanese": "{道|みち}に{飛|と}び{出|だ}してきた{子供|こども}を{危|あや}うく{轢|ひ}きそうになった。",
      "english": "I nearly ran over a child who darted out into the road.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: Transitive godan verb. Xを{轢|ひ}く. Always describes a vehicle hitting a person or animal.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {人|ひと}を{轢|ひ}く: to run over a person\n- {車|くるま}に{轢|ひ}かれる: to be hit by a car (passive)\n- {轢|ひ}き{逃|に}げ: hit-and-run\n\nUSAGE:\n{轢|ひ}く shares its reading with {引|ひ}く (to pull), {弾|ひ}く (to play a stringed instrument), and {挽|ひ}く (to grind), but is written with its own kanji and used only for vehicle accidents.",
